CHOICE: 128 mults/PE (15 PEs, 1920 DSPs) -- the only size meeting 30 fps at 300 MHz with margin (33.7); 64 falls to 26.0 fps because TN=4 forces L3 to outer mode (32cy/step vs 4cy/step in dot), and 256 meets 30 only barely (31.5 fps) while wasting half its lanes on C_out=8. 128 also halves the control vs 64 (15 PEs vs 30 buffer slices / scoreboard entries).

