VCU128 decode roofline (HBM-bound, not compute-bound):
  HBM 460 GB/s @ 300 MHz = 1533 weight bytes/cycle; one MAC consumes one weight byte/cycle, so ~1533 MACs/cycle saturate HBM
  the 15x128 config has 1920 MACs/cycle -- already above the saturation point, so the PE count is NOT scaled up for the VU37P
  7B INT8: 65.7 tok/s roofline (fits one board)
  13B INT4: 70.8 tok/s roofline (fits one board)
  13B INT8: 35.4 tok/s roofline (needs 2 boards, 16 GB HBM)
  vu37p 1080p @300 MHz: 33.7 fps (MEETS 30fps)

